* (=|-) 42.4. [feature] Notifications {* 42.4}

  Push notifications for real-time events and scheduled email digests
  for activity summaries. Pluggable delivery channels with per-user
  preference management.

  /Partially blocked: {* 42.11.5} Legal — Privacy Policy Review must
  complete before Validation sign-off can proceed./

  Pre-requisites:
  - (x) {* 42.1} Authentication — user identity and push token registration
  - (x) {* 42.6.6} Message Queue — async notification dispatch
  - (x) {* 42.6.7} Secrets — push provider credentials (APNs, FCM)


** (-) 42.4.1. Stage 1 — Push Notifications {* 42.4.1}

*** (x) 42.4.1.1. Design {* 42.4.1.1}
    User stories:
    - /As a user, I want to receive push notifications for new messages,
      shared notes, and account events, so that I stay informed without
      checking the app constantly./
    - /As a user, I want to control which notifications I receive and
      how, so that I'm not overwhelmed by alerts I don't care about./

    Artifacts:
    - Notification event taxonomy (message, share, mention, system, security)
    - Delivery architecture: event → queue → dispatcher → provider (APNs/FCM)
    - Database schema: `push_tokens`, `notification_preferences`,
      `notification_log` tables

*** (-) 42.4.1.2. Implementation {* 42.4.1.2}

**** (x) 42.4.1.2.1. Backend {* 42.4.1.2.1}
     - (x) Push token registration and lifecycle management
       - AC: stores device token + platform (iOS/Android) per user
       - AC: deregisters stale tokens on provider feedback (invalid/expired)
       - AC: user can have multiple active tokens (multiple devices)
     - (x) Notification dispatcher with channel routing
       - AC: consumes events from SQS; routes to APNs or FCM based on token
       - AC: retries with exponential backoff (3 attempts, 1s/5s/30s)
       - AC: dead-letter queue for permanently failed deliveries
     - (x) Notification event API (internal, service-to-service)
       - AC: accepts event type, recipient user ID, payload, and priority
       - AC: high-priority events bypass batching; normal events may batch
     - (x) User preference management endpoints
       - AC: per-category toggle (messages, shares, mentions, system)
       - AC: quiet hours setting (start/end time + timezone)
       - AC: preferences checked before dispatch; suppressed events logged
     - (x) Notification log with read/unread tracking
       - AC: persists all dispatched notifications for 90 days
       - AC: mark-as-read endpoint (single and bulk)
       - AC: unread count endpoint for badge display
     - (x) Rate limiting and deduplication
       - AC: max 30 notifications/min per user (burst protection)
       - AC: duplicate detection within 60s window (same event type + target)

**** (x) 42.4.1.2.2. Frontend {* 42.4.1.2.2}
     - (x) Notification centre dropdown with grouped events
       - AC: grouped by date (Today, Yesterday, Earlier)
       - AC: unread items visually distinct; click marks as read
       - AC: "Mark all as read" action in header
     - (x) Notification badge on navigation (bell icon)
       - AC: shows unread count; updates in real-time via WebSocket
       - AC: badge disappears when count reaches 0
     - (x) Browser push notification permission flow
       - AC: prompt shown after first meaningful action (not on page load)
       - AC: "Not now" delays re-prompt for 7 days
       - AC: denied state shows in-app notification centre only
     - (x) Notification preference settings page
       - AC: toggle per category; quiet hours with time pickers
       - AC: test notification button to verify delivery
     - (x) Click-through routing from notification to source content
       - AC: clicking a message notification opens that conversation
       - AC: clicking a share notification opens the shared note

**** (-) 42.4.1.2.3. Mobile {* 42.4.1.2.3}
     - (x) Push token registration on app launch
       - AC: requests notification permission on first launch
       - AC: registers token with backend; refreshes on token change
     - (x) Notification payload handling (foreground + background)
       - AC: foreground: in-app banner (not system notification)
       - AC: background: system notification with sound and badge
     - (-) Rich notification content (image preview, action buttons)
       - AC: message notifications show sender avatar
       - AC: action buttons: Reply, Mark as Read (without opening app)
       - AC: notification grouping per conversation (iOS) / channel (Android)
     - ( ) Notification preference screen (native)
       - AC: mirrors web settings; syncs via API on save
       - AC: links to system notification settings for channel control
     - ( ) Notification history screen
       - AC: scrollable list of past notifications with read/unread state
       - AC: swipe to dismiss individual notifications

*** (-) 42.4.1.3. Verification {* 42.4.1.3}
    - (x) Backend: 7 test suites (token lifecycle, dispatcher, routing,
          preferences, rate limiting, dedup, notification log)
    - (x) Frontend: 5 test suites (notification centre, badge, browser push,
          preferences, click-through routing)
    - (-) Mobile: 2 of 5 suites completed (token registration, payload
          handling; pending: rich content, preferences, history)
    - ( ) Integration: E2E notification flow — trigger event → dispatch
          → receive on web and mobile

*** ( ) 42.4.1.4. Validation {* 42.4.1.4}
    - ( ) QA scenarios: delivery across providers, preference suppression,
          quiet hours, rate limiting, deduplication
    - ( ) Performance: dispatch latency <3s from event to device delivery
    - ( ) Cross-platform: notification state synced (read on web =
          badge cleared on mobile)


** ( ) 42.4.2. Stage 2 — Email Digests {* 42.4.2}

*** ( ) 42.4.2.1. Design {* 42.4.2.1}
    User stories:
    - /As a user, I want to receive a daily or weekly email summary of
      activity I missed, so that I stay informed even when I'm away from
      the app for extended periods./

    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.4.1} Stage 1 — Push Notifications (preference system)
    - ( ) {* 42.6.8} CDN — email asset hosting (images, styles)

*** ( ) 42.4.2.2. Implementation {* 42.4.2.2}

**** ( ) 42.4.2.2.1. Backend {* 42.4.2.2.1}
     - ( ) Digest scheduler (daily at user's preferred time, weekly on Monday)
       - AC: scheduled via cron; skips users with no unread activity
       - AC: respects user timezone for delivery time
     - ( ) Activity aggregation service
       - AC: collects unread messages, new shares, mentions since last digest
       - AC: groups by source (chat, notes, system) with counts and previews
     - ( ) Email template engine with responsive HTML
       - AC: renders with user name, activity sections, action links
       - AC: plain-text fallback for email clients without HTML support
     - ( ) Digest preference endpoints (frequency, enabled/disabled)
       - AC: options: daily, weekly, disabled; defaults to weekly
     - ( ) Unsubscribe flow (one-click from email footer)
       - AC: unsubscribe link disables digest without requiring login
       - AC: re-enable available from notification settings page

**** ( ) 42.4.2.2.2. Frontend {* 42.4.2.2.2}
     - ( ) Digest preference controls on notification settings page
       - AC: frequency dropdown (daily/weekly/disabled)
       - AC: preferred delivery time picker (for daily digest)
     - ( ) Digest preview ("see what your next digest will look like")
       - AC: renders sample digest in modal using current activity data

**** ( ) 42.4.2.2.3. Mobile {* 42.4.2.2.3}
     - ( ) Digest preference controls on notification settings screen
       - AC: mirrors web settings; syncs on save
     - ( ) Deep link handling from digest email links
       - AC: tapping activity link in email opens relevant screen in app
       - AC: falls back to web if app not installed

*** ( ) 42.4.2.3. Verification {* 42.4.2.3}
    - ( ) Backend: scheduler, aggregation, template rendering, unsubscribe
    - ( ) Frontend: preference controls, preview rendering
    - ( ) Mobile: preferences, deep link handling
    - ( ) Integration: digest generation → email delivery → link click-through

*** ( ) 42.4.2.4. Validation {* 42.4.2.4}
    - ( ) QA scenarios: daily/weekly generation, timezone handling,
          unsubscribe, re-enable, empty-activity skip
    - ( ) Email rendering: verified across Gmail, Outlook, Apple Mail
